     "text": "```python\nfrom pedantic import validate, count_calls\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Optional\n\n@validate\n@count_calls\ndef shortest_path(graph: dict, start: str, end: str) -> Optional[List[str]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the shortest path from start to end in an undirected graph.\n\n    Args:\n        graph: A dictionary where keys are node identifiers and values are lists of connected nodes.\n        start: The starting node.\n        end: The target node.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of nodes representing the shortest path from start to end, or None if no path exists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if start not in graph or end not in graph:\n        return None\n\n    visited = set()\n    queue = [(start, [start])]\n\n    while queue:\n        current_node, path = queue.pop(0)\n        if current_node == end:\n            return path\n        if current_node in visited:\n            continue\n        visited.add(current_node)\n        for neighbor in graph[current_node]:\n            if neighbor not in visited:\n                queue.append((neighbor, path + [neighbor]))\n\n    return None\n```",
